invariant: INV-7
file: quic.c
catches: quic_loop_test
reason: ch_quic_key_update advances the 1-RTT secrets under the original
  version's key update label, "quic ku" where a switched session owes
  "quicv2 ku" (rfc9369.txt:167-174), so its next keys are not the
  server's and the first packet after the update opens at neither end.
  test/quic_loop_version.h updates the keys of a client that switched to
  version 2 and requires its next packet to open at the server.

--- old
    uint32_t version = q->t.quic_negotiated_version;
    quic_keys_update(CH_CFG_CPU(q->t.cfg), q->t.wr_secret, &q->app_tx, version);
--- new
    uint32_t version = q->t.quic_negotiated_version;
    quic_keys_update(CH_CFG_CPU(q->t.cfg), q->t.wr_secret, &q->app_tx,
                     q->t.cfg.quic_original_version);
